## Rule of the Court (DIFC RDC 38.40 + Practice Direction No. 4 of 2017)
##
## Source 1: Rules of the DIFC Courts, Part 38 (Costs), specifically RDC
## 38.40 — costs payable within 14 days of the date of the order assessing
## them, unless the Court orders otherwise.
##
## Source 2: DIFC Courts Practice Direction No. 4 of 2017 — Interest on
## Judgments, prescribing interest at 9% per annum on unpaid judgment
## sums from the date of the order until payment in full.
##
## This file expresses the rule applied in:
##   ARB 008/2026 — Oberlin v Ovidiu
##   Order with Reasons of H.E. Justice Shamlan Al Sawalehi, 26 March 2026.
## Operative paragraphs 2 and 3:
##   "2. The Defendant shall pay the Costs Award within 14 days of the
##       date of this Order, pursuant to RDC 38.40.
##    3. In the event that the Defendant fails to pay the Costs Award
##       within 14 days of the date of this Order, interest shall accrue
##       at the rate of 9% per annum from the date of this Order until
##       payment in full, in accordance with Practice Direction No. 4
##       of 2017."
##
## The rule has a deferred-conditional shape: nothing accrues so long as
## payment is made within the 14-day window. If the deadline is missed
## the trigger fires and interest is computed retroactively from the
## date of the order — not from the deadline. The predicate below
## captures that asymmetry directly.
##
## Catala 1.1.0 notes:
##   - Date subtraction returns a `duration`. We convert to `decimal`
##     number of days via `(d1 - d2) / 1 day`.
##   - For an integer-N-days duration in a variable, use `N * (1 day)`.

```catala
declaration structure CostsAwardOrder:
  data principal_aed content decimal
  data order_date content date
  data deadline_days content integer
  data interest_rate_pa content decimal

declaration structure PaymentStatus:
  data as_of content date
  data paid content boolean
  data payment_date content date

declaration structure AmountOwed:
  data deadline content date
  data in_breach content boolean
  data days_accrued content decimal
  data interest_accrued_aed content decimal
  data total_owed_aed content decimal

declaration scope OutstandingObligation:
  input order content CostsAwardOrder
  input status content PaymentStatus
  output owed content AmountOwed

scope OutstandingObligation:
  definition owed equals
    let deadline equals order.order_date + (order.deadline_days * (1 day)) in
    let reference_date equals
      if status.paid then status.payment_date else status.as_of
    in
    let in_breach equals reference_date > deadline in
    let days equals
      if in_breach
      then ((reference_date - order.order_date) / 1 day)
      else 0.0
    in
    let interest equals
      order.principal_aed * order.interest_rate_pa * (days / 365.0)
    in
    AmountOwed {
      -- deadline: deadline
      -- in_breach: in_breach
      -- days_accrued: days
      -- interest_accrued_aed: interest
      -- total_owed_aed: order.principal_aed + interest
    }
```

## Test — facts of ARB 008/2026

```catala
#[test] declaration scope TestOberlinPaidOnTime:
  obligation scope OutstandingObligation
  output owed content AmountOwed

scope TestOberlinPaidOnTime:
  definition obligation.order equals CostsAwardOrder {
    -- principal_aed: 76785.81
    -- order_date: |2026-03-26|
    -- deadline_days: 14
    -- interest_rate_pa: 0.09
  }
  definition obligation.status equals PaymentStatus {
    -- as_of: |2026-04-08|
    -- paid: true
    -- payment_date: |2026-04-08|
  }
  definition owed equals obligation.owed

  assertion owed.in_breach = false
  assertion owed.total_owed_aed = 76785.81

#[test] declaration scope TestOberlinUnpaid61Days:
  obligation scope OutstandingObligation
  output owed content AmountOwed

scope TestOberlinUnpaid61Days:
  definition obligation.order equals CostsAwardOrder {
    -- principal_aed: 76785.81
    -- order_date: |2026-03-26|
    -- deadline_days: 14
    -- interest_rate_pa: 0.09
  }
  definition obligation.status equals PaymentStatus {
    -- as_of: |2026-05-26|
    -- paid: false
    -- payment_date: |2026-05-26|
  }
  definition owed equals obligation.owed

  assertion owed.in_breach = true
  assertion owed.days_accrued = 61.0
```
